-y}{{x}^{2}}=\\frac{1\\cdot 1-(-2)}{{1}^{2}}=3 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=-2+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=1+\\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these values to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $3$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $-\\frac{3}{2}$ |  |  | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |  |  |\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nWe compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy,$ ${z}^{′}$ and $Δz$ (using the values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the second row), and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}},$ ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and ${z}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{xz-y}{{x}^{2}}=\\frac{(3/2)\\cdot (5/2)-(-3/2)}{(-3/2)^{2}}=\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx=\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{7}{6} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{5}{4}=-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{7}{6}=\\frac{11}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these values to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $3$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $-\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{3}$ | $\\frac{7}{6}$ |\n| $2$ | $-\\frac{1}{4}$ |  |  | $\\frac{11}{3}$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(2)≈-\\frac{1}{4}$\nand\n${y}^{′}(2)=z(2)≈\\frac{11}{3}.$" 13194139535839 true] [17592186221928 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535839 true] [17592186221928 1100 "Consider the foll