-1$ |  |  |\n\nNext, we compute both ${y}^{′}$ and ${z}^{′}$ according to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=-1 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{3x-2yz}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3+2}{1} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $-1$ |  | $-1$ | $5$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ and $Δz$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $5$ | $5$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ and $Δz$ to $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+(-1)=0 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=(-1)+5=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $-1$ | $5$ | $5$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ |  |  | $4$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(2)≈0$\nand ${y}^{′}(2)=z(2)≈4.$" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369378 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535839 true] [17592186369378 1111 #uuid "86f87f4c-67e4-584a-8b28-659e0826615f" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369379 1034 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535839 true] [17592186369379 1111 #uuid "53df8caa-11c0-5ed7-b820-3fe4e58e929d" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369380 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369381 13194139535839 true] [17592186369380 1017 #edb/ref 17592186369