g to the given rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=0 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+4xz}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot {1}^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 0}{1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |  | $0$ | $2$ |  |\n\nNext, we compute $Δy$ and $Δz$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0 \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n\nTo get the new values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the *next* row, we add $Δx$ to $x,$ $Δy$ to $y,$ and $Δz$ to $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=1+0=1 \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=0+2=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these values to our table in a new row gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $2$ | $1$ |  |  | $2$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n$y(2)≈1$\nand\n${y}^{′}(2)=z(2)≈2.$" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369427 13194139535839 true] [17592186369426 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535839 true] [17592186369426 1041 "field-1" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369426 1104 #edb/ref 17592186369427 13194139535839 true] [17592186369426 1110 #uuid "e7f49825-68be-5e9c-a991-309d843d5da2" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369427 1034 "1" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535839 true] [17592186369427 1111 #uuid "6feb15e3-072f-5c73-b1ef-d5c785fbe36e" 13194139535839 true] [17592186369428 1000 #edb/ref 17592186369429 13194139535839 true] [17592186369428 1040 #edb/ref