\text{new}},$ ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and ${z}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=1 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{2y-xz}{{x}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}}=3 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=1+\\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these values to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $3$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |  |  | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |  |  |\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nWe compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy,$ ${z}^{′}$ and $Δz$ (using the values of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ in the second row), and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}},$ ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and ${z}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =z=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ {z}^{′} & =\\frac{2y-xz}{{x}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}=\\frac{(\\frac{5}{4})}{(\\frac{9}{4})}=\\frac{5}{9} \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ Δz & ={z}^{′}\\cdot Δx=\\frac{5}{9}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{5}{18} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{5}{4}=\\frac{15}{4} \\\\ {z}_{\\text{new}} & =z+Δz=\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{5}{18}=\\frac{25}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add these values to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $3$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{9}$ | $\\frac{5}{18}$ |\n| $2$ | $\\frac{15}{4}$ |  |  | $\\frac{25}{9}$ |  